Decode the test split with the configured testing.forward_type.

Applies to: Atrewin/SignXmDA b6e2ca4ea81cab41cf858e1d0ce948a778cb09a5 after
0001-gloss-decoding-mirror-training.patch.

Execution bug. prediction_XmDA.test() passes
forward_type=cfg["testing"]["forward_type"] to both dev decoding passes but
not to the final test pass, which then falls back to validate_on_data's
default "sign". For a forward_type=gloss teacher, whose upstream config sets
the test split to the training pickle to produce KD references, the training
set is therefore translated by feeding sign features into a model trained on
glosses. Run preflight-phoenix14t-teacher-attempt-2: dev BLEU-4 19.83, but on
the training set BLEU-4 0.76 with WER 100 (all deletions), and 5,012 of 7,096
translations start with "in der neuen woche".

Behavior: unchanged for every model tested with testing.forward_type sign
(all baselines and the mixup/kd/xmda students); gloss teachers decode the test
split on their gloss input, as their dev passes already do. The same omission
in test_model_average() is left alone because training_XmDA never calls it.

